.TH GOTO-DIFF "1" "March 1, 2026" "goto-diff-6.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
goto\-diff \- Syntactic diff of goto binaries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goto\-diff
.RI [ options ]
.I old new
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgoto\-diff\fR compares two GOTO binaries (as produced by \fBgoto\-cc\fR(1))
and reports syntactic differences in their GOTO program representations.
It can produce unified diffs and dependency-based change-impact analyses.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Diff options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-goto\-functions\fR
Display the GOTO program instructions for all functions.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-goto\-functions\fR
List the names of all functions without showing their bodies.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-properties\fR
List all properties without running analysis.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-loops\fR
List all loops in both programs.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR | \fB\-\-unified\fR
output unified diff
.TP
\fB\-\-change\-impact\fR
Output unified diff with both forward and backward dependencies.
.TP
\fB\-\-forward\-impact\fR
Output unified diff with forward dependencies only.
.TP
\fB\-\-backward\-impact\fR
Output unified diff with backward dependencies only.
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\-output\fR
output dependencies in compact mode
.SS "Program instrumentation options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-bounds\-check\fR
Insert assertions that array and buffer accesses are within bounds.
.TP
\fB\-\-pointer\-check\fR
Insert assertions that pointers are valid when dereferenced.
.TP
\fB\-\-memory\-leak\-check\fR
Insert assertions that all dynamically allocated memory is freed before
program termination.
.TP
\fB\-\-memory\-cleanup\-check\fR
Insert assertions that all dynamically allocated memory is explicitly
freed before program termination.
.TP
\fB\-\-div\-by\-zero\-check\fR
Insert assertions that integer division and modulo do not divide by zero.
.TP
\fB\-\-float\-div\-by\-zero\-check\fR
Insert assertions that floating-point division does not divide by zero.
.TP
\fB\-\-signed\-overflow\-check\fR
Insert assertions that signed integer arithmetic does not overflow.
.TP
\fB\-\-unsigned\-overflow\-check\fR
Insert assertions that unsigned integer arithmetic does not wrap around.
.TP
\fB\-\-pointer\-overflow\-check\fR
Insert assertions that pointer arithmetic does not overflow.
.TP
\fB\-\-conversion\-check\fR
Insert assertions that values can be faithfully represented after a
type cast.
.TP
\fB\-\-undefined\-shift\-check\fR
Insert assertions that shift amounts are non-negative and less than the
bit-width of the shifted type.
.TP
\fB\-\-float\-overflow\-check\fR
Insert assertions that floating-point operations do not produce infinity.
.TP
\fB\-\-nan\-check\fR
Insert assertions that floating-point operations do not produce NaN.
.TP
\fB\-\-enum\-range\-check\fR
Insert assertions that enum-typed expressions hold values within the
defined range.
.TP
\fB\-\-pointer\-primitive\-check\fR
Insert assertions that all pointers passed to pointer primitives are
valid or null.
.TP
\fB\-\-retain\-trivial\-checks\fR
Keep checks that are trivially true.
.TP
\fB\-\-error\-label\fR \fIlabel\fR
Insert an assertion that the given \fIlabel\fR is unreachable.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-built\-in\-assertions\fR
Ignore assertions in the built-in C library models.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-assertions\fR
Ignore all user-written assertions.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-assumptions\fR
Ignore all assumptions.
.TP
\fB\-\-assert\-to\-assume\fR
Convert all user assertions to assumptions.
.TP
\fB\-\-cover\fR CC
create test\-suite with coverage criterion CC,
where CC is one of assertion[s], assume[s],
branch[es], condition[s], cover, decision[s],
location[s], or mcdc
.TP
\fB\-\-cover\-failed\-assertions\fR
do not stop coverage checking at failed assertions
(this is the default for \fB\-\-cover\fR assertions)
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-test\-suite\fR
print test suite for coverage criterion (requires \fB\-\-cover\fR)
.SS "Other options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show version and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-json\-ui\fR
use JSON\-formatted output
.TP
\fB\-\-flush\fR
flush every line of output
.TP
\fB\-\-verbosity\fR \fIn\fR
verbosity level
.TP
\fB\-\-timestamp\fR [\fBmonotonic\fR|\fBwall\fR]
Print microsecond\-precision timestamps.  \fBmonotonic\fR: stamps increase
monotonically.  \fBwall\fR: ISO\-8601 wall clock timestamps.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMPDIR
All CProver tools honor this variable when creating temporary files and
directories.
.SH BUGS
If you encounter a problem please create an issue at
.B https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/issues
